cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the draft by its commit or, once a release is archived on Zenodo,
  by the version DOI, so the words you cite are the words that were there.
title: "Own the Machine: a draft EU Regulation on citizens' participation in automated productivity gains"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Vanheeswijck
    given-names: David
    country: BE
repository-code: "https://github.com/ownthemachine/own-the-machine"
url: "https://ownthemachine.eu"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
keywords:
  - European Union
  - European Citizens' Initiative
  - automation
  - capital ownership
  - universal dividend
  - draft regulation
abstract: >-
  A complete draft EU Regulation, with explanatory memorandum, objections
  file and evidence base, requiring undertakings whose output is
  substantially decoupled from employment to issue, once, a non-voting
  warrant over 3 % of their fully diluted capital to a European Citizens'
  Capital Reserve held for all Union citizens. Drafted in the open as the
  basis for a possible European Citizens' Initiative; every review verdict,
  failed rounds included, is committed alongside the text.
